### Describe the bug

Private fields should be checked for private access.

### Input code

```typescript
class Foo {
	#bar;

#privateMethod() {
    return 'hello world';
  }
}

var f = new Foo();
foo.#bar;
foo.#privateMethod();
```


### Config

```json
{
  "jsc": {
    "target": "es5",
    "parser": {
      "syntax": "ecmascript"
    }
  },
  "module": {
    "type": "commonjs"
  },
  "sourceMaps": true,
  "isModule": false
}
```


### Playground link

https://play.swc.rs/?version=1.2.172&code=H4sIAAAAAAAAA0vOSSwuVnDLz1eo5uJUTkossubiUi4oyixLLEn1TS3JyE%2FR0ARKKQBBUWpJaVGegnpGak5OvkJ5flFOiro1UKaWq5aLqyyxSCFNwVYhL7UcZJqGpjVXWn6%2BHsREMAvNUGsARdmggXoAAAA%3D&config=H4sIAAAAAAAAAy3LMQ6DMBBE0btM7TaN78AhVpsNAmFs7awlEPLdA1GqXzz9CysV%2BUKIzxbIML6Q0MRp%2FgDPPeR4QItQfWmBMRJKfffNfuvZ7kJrKXVfiRtZu6tN0ogc3i1h4fQfPrLRxhe4j3L6eQAAAA%3D%3D

### Expected behavior

Syntax error that private name cannot be accessed.

Eg:

```
  x Illegal access to private class property.
    ,----
 14 | foo.#bar;
    : ^^^^^^^^
    `----

  x Illegal access to private class property.
    ,----
 15 | foo.#privateMethod();
    : ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    `----
```

### Actual behavior

Gets transpiled to the following:

```
...
var Foo = function Foo() {
    "use strict";
    _classCallCheck(this, Foo);
    _classPrivateMethodInit(this, _privateMethod);
    _classPrivateFieldInit(this, _bar, {
        writable: true,
        value: void 0
    });
};
var f = new Foo();
foo.#bar;
foo.#privateMethod();
```

### Version

1.2.160

### Additional context

_No response_

